### API Testing Guide for RentAnything Backend

This file contains requests to test the authentication and incident reporting flow.
You can use the **REST Client** extension in VS Code to run these requests directly.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@phone = +94771234567

### 1. Register Individual User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register/individual
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "address": "123 Main St, Colombo"
}

### 2. Login (Triggers OTP)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}"
}

### 3. Verify OTP (Get JWT Token)
# @name verifyOtp
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "otp": "1111"
}

### Save the access token from the response above
@accessToken = {{verifyOtp.response.body.access_token}}

### 4. Create Incident Report
# Note: You need a valid rentalId in your database to run this successfully.
POST {{baseUrl}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rentalId": 1,
  "description": "The rented professional camera has a small scratch on the lens after return.",
  "media": [
    {
      "mediaType": "image",
      "mediaUrl": "https://storage.rentanything.com/incidents/scratch1.jpg"
    }
  ]
}

### 5. Get All Incidents
GET {{baseUrl}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6. Get Specific Incident
GET {{baseUrl}}/incidents/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. Get All Rentals (To find a valid rentalId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
